WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:04.270
For instance,
even if those arms of yours

00:04.270 --> 00:07.100
Become entwined in chains

00:07.100 --> 00:10.540
For instance,
even if this space we live in

00:10.540 --> 00:14.910
Someday will burn completely down

00:14.910 --> 00:21.040
Keep believing in hope, if nothing else

00:22.320 --> 00:26.580
In the shadows of glimmering stars

00:28.390 --> 00:32.660
There is a world governed by darkness

00:34.460 --> 00:38.960
Just one life that is out there

00:40.470 --> 00:45.740
If you keep it entrapped there,
lonely boy

00:46.540 --> 00:52.310
The reason that we met each other here

00:52.310 --> 00:58.650
Must surely exist

00:58.650 --> 01:01.920
For instance,
even if sorrow takes you

01:01.920 --> 01:04.860
And you're about to collapse under it

01:04.860 --> 01:08.200
For instance,
if my chest can become

01:08.200 --> 01:12.570
A power to hold you and keep you there

01:12.570 --> 01:16.970
I'm sure that even
tomorrow we can survive

01:36.860 --> 01:39.190
Our ship has been
completely swallowed up.

01:39.190 --> 01:40.800
The bridge, residential quarters,

01:40.800 --> 01:43.800
and the engine room have
been completely engulfed.

01:43.800 --> 01:45.500
Fortunately, the Dread platform

01:45.500 --> 01:47.540
and the Reg system suffered no damage.

01:47.540 --> 01:50.970
Right now, we're cleaning
up and installing the database.

01:50.970 --> 01:55.340
The spread of Paksis Pragma
seems to be reaching its peak now.

01:55.340 --> 01:56.680
The bridge has stopped sliding

01:56.680 --> 01:59.580
and is currently jutting
out into the ship's garden.

01:59.580 --> 02:02.420
All changes in the ship
have stopped for now.

02:02.420 --> 02:03.350
Meia.

02:03.350 --> 02:04.010
Right.

02:04.620 --> 02:07.690
The three Dreads that were
swallowed and transformed

02:07.690 --> 02:10.430
by the Paksis no longer
fit in our platforms.

02:10.430 --> 02:13.700
We modified the men's
cargo bay to store them.

02:13.700 --> 02:15.660
We found out during this process,

02:15.660 --> 02:18.930
that this ship hasn't been
used in quite a long time.

02:18.930 --> 02:21.470
Circuits and cables are decayed.

02:21.470 --> 02:23.840
The problem is our current location.

02:23.840 --> 02:27.140
It's unbelievable,
but we're a long way from Mejale,

02:27.140 --> 02:29.740
in a completely
different nebula, in fact.

02:29.740 --> 02:32.270
In terms of time,
we are about 270 days away.

02:33.410 --> 02:37.190
Why did something like this happen?

02:37.190 --> 02:39.890
And? Any data about the enemy?

02:39.890 --> 02:40.820
Yes...

02:40.820 --> 02:44.130
We were shorthanded so
we sent volunteers to investigate.

02:44.130 --> 02:45.820
Volunteers?

02:48.100 --> 02:48.760
Wow!

02:48.760 --> 02:50.670
Amazing! Amazing!

02:50.670 --> 02:53.030
Hey, isn't that an Adamsky-shaped UFO?

02:53.030 --> 02:55.270
Hey, are you watching?

02:55.270 --> 02:56.440
How is it?

02:56.440 --> 02:57.910
I think I'm fine now.

02:57.910 --> 02:59.410
Thanks.

02:59.410 --> 03:02.010
Hey, can you turn
on the air conditioning?

03:02.010 --> 03:03.480
It's 28 degrees here!

03:03.480 --> 03:04.750
Don't complain!

03:04.750 --> 03:06.110
It's over 30 degrees here!

03:06.110 --> 03:07.480
No response here.

03:07.480 --> 03:09.210
Parfet, what about there?

03:10.890 --> 03:12.450
This is an old system.

03:12.450 --> 03:14.660
Is this a prototype?

03:14.660 --> 03:16.460
It's no wonder it burst.

03:16.460 --> 03:18.930
Hey, hurry up and help out over here!

03:18.930 --> 03:19.630
Beep!

03:19.630 --> 03:22.160
- Hey, don't touch me!
- Oh, geez! Stay still!

03:22.160 --> 03:24.860
We can't seriously
get any data like this!

03:26.470 --> 03:29.400
And so, while taking
over the enemy ship,

03:29.400 --> 03:32.470
Magno's family faces a new crisis!

03:32.470 --> 03:33.510
Pai!

03:33.510 --> 03:35.610
If you're bored, then help us!

03:35.610 --> 03:37.080
I'm not bored!

03:37.080 --> 03:39.250
Wait! We're getting on!

03:39.250 --> 03:40.650
You're fooling around again!

03:40.650 --> 03:42.680
Oh, sheesh!

03:42.680 --> 03:45.390
Moving! Moving!

03:45.390 --> 03:47.990
Aren't you glad our
rooms were all right?

03:47.990 --> 03:48.960
Ribbit!

03:48.960 --> 03:50.330
This pisses me off...

03:50.330 --> 03:52.630
You're making this heat worse.

03:52.630 --> 03:54.500
What's this rope?

03:54.500 --> 03:57.270
This elevator is still temporary!

03:57.270 --> 03:59.230
I'm not responsible if it falls!

03:59.230 --> 04:00.970
Bye!

04:00.970 --> 04:02.670
W-Wait, you're kidding, right?

04:02.670 --> 04:03.400
Pai!

04:06.310 --> 04:08.210
Dammit, what the hell!

04:08.210 --> 04:11.250
Now all we have left are these guys.

04:11.250 --> 04:15.280
We should use them till we
understand the systems on this ship.

04:15.280 --> 04:16.180
Yeah...

04:16.180 --> 04:18.520
I've never seen anything
like it before.

04:18.520 --> 04:21.390
It seemed as though
this ship had a will of its own.

04:21.390 --> 04:23.020
It makes me shiver.

04:23.020 --> 04:25.630
Boy, did it make me shiver!

04:25.630 --> 04:27.230
My allies falling one after another,

04:27.230 --> 04:29.630
and before I knew
it I was the only one left.

04:29.630 --> 04:32.330
And I thought,
it's easier just to die here.

04:32.330 --> 04:34.170
But my duty was to live on,

04:34.170 --> 04:38.440
and regain control of
this ship from those women!

04:38.440 --> 04:40.510
Fortunately, I have gained two comrades.

04:40.510 --> 04:41.780
Well?

04:41.780 --> 04:43.180
Geez...

04:43.180 --> 04:47.480
I thought I was able to change,
but this is how it is in the end?

04:47.480 --> 04:48.480
But...

04:48.480 --> 04:49.350
What the hell...

04:49.350 --> 04:51.020
...was that thing?

04:51.020 --> 04:52.920
Where did they make
a Vanguard like that?

04:52.920 --> 04:54.290
Why does it fuse with a woman?

04:54.290 --> 04:55.420
Like I know!

04:55.420 --> 04:58.590
But before that,
how dare you sock me before!

04:58.590 --> 04:59.530
Whoa!

04:59.530 --> 05:01.060
Don't get angry.

05:01.060 --> 05:02.960
I had your best interests in mind!

05:02.960 --> 05:05.130
You're such an annoying chatterbox!

05:05.130 --> 05:06.870
It's hot enough in here!

05:06.870 --> 05:08.030
He's just worried.

05:08.900 --> 05:11.810
He's just taking his mind
off of things by talking.

05:11.810 --> 05:12.970
Forgive him.

05:12.970 --> 05:14.910
Y-You really are sharp.

05:14.910 --> 05:16.810
Nothing less from an elite student.

05:16.810 --> 05:18.110
So how about it?

05:18.110 --> 05:20.620
With my speaking skills
and your brain,

05:20.620 --> 05:21.920
we can easily take the women.

05:21.920 --> 05:23.320
What will happen?

05:23.320 --> 05:24.290
Oh, uh...

05:24.290 --> 05:25.820
Nothing. We're just talking.

05:25.820 --> 05:27.620
I'd love to listen in.

05:27.620 --> 05:29.180
I want you to come with me.

05:30.390 --> 05:32.190
I'd love to if it's just talking.

05:35.930 --> 05:39.420
This place is more like
a giant factory than a spaceship.

05:40.300 --> 05:42.300
Wow, this is amazing!

05:42.300 --> 05:43.540
Look at that!

05:43.540 --> 05:46.470
So, any clues?

05:46.470 --> 05:50.310
We're searching the database,
but when it's this huge...

05:50.310 --> 05:51.680
Hey, hey!

05:51.680 --> 05:53.450
Can I go look over there?

05:53.450 --> 05:54.820
No!

05:54.820 --> 05:56.350
We're working now!

05:56.350 --> 05:57.380
Stop this thing!

05:59.390 --> 06:00.320
What?

06:00.320 --> 06:02.190
I brought our navigator here.

06:02.190 --> 06:03.660
I'll be right there.

06:03.660 --> 06:06.130
Well, I ask you to keep it up, Gascogne.

06:06.130 --> 06:06.790
Sure.

06:14.140 --> 06:16.000
H-Hello.

06:16.000 --> 06:17.810
You wanted something from me?

06:17.810 --> 06:19.670
Yes, that.

06:21.010 --> 06:22.580
It doesn't move at all.

06:22.580 --> 06:24.170
How did you do it?

06:28.320 --> 06:30.420
Of course, that can't be helped.

06:30.420 --> 06:33.290
I'll show you.

06:33.290 --> 06:34.820
Listen closely.

06:34.820 --> 06:36.160
This is a male ship.

06:36.160 --> 06:37.930
Only men can move it.

06:37.930 --> 06:41.360
You are all here because
I was fortunately on this ship.

06:41.360 --> 06:45.230
In other words,
I am indispensable to all of you...

06:48.940 --> 06:51.430
I really don't understand
this system after all.

06:54.010 --> 06:55.340
That's about...

06:55.340 --> 06:55.870
What?

07:01.320 --> 07:02.750
What?

07:02.750 --> 07:04.320
W-What's wrong now?

07:04.320 --> 07:05.990
The system suddenly booted up!

07:05.990 --> 07:07.590
Checking target destination.

07:07.590 --> 07:09.660
What did you do?

07:09.660 --> 07:11.190
W-Wait just a minute!

07:11.190 --> 07:12.920
I'll find out.

07:18.930 --> 07:20.870
I copied the data.

07:20.870 --> 07:22.900
Captain?

07:22.900 --> 07:23.870
Ms. Gasco...

07:23.870 --> 07:25.710
Dita!

07:25.710 --> 07:27.400
Please, copy!

07:28.580 --> 07:29.610
Release the markers.

07:29.610 --> 07:30.880
Roger.

07:30.880 --> 07:32.210
Gasco...

07:33.350 --> 07:35.010
Ezra! What's wrong?

07:36.950 --> 07:38.350
Who are you?

07:38.350 --> 07:40.350
What are you trying to make me do?

07:40.350 --> 07:42.260
What is that huge robot?

07:42.260 --> 07:43.830
Did you plan it all?

07:43.830 --> 07:44.810
What about me?

07:50.530 --> 07:51.900
Hibiki.

07:51.900 --> 07:53.000
Gramps...

07:53.000 --> 07:55.000
Go to the city, Hibiki.

07:55.000 --> 07:56.270
W-Why?

07:56.270 --> 07:58.740
To know your own self.

08:00.410 --> 08:02.080
I already know enough!

08:02.080 --> 08:04.850
No, you don't know.

08:04.850 --> 08:07.870
Your friends are mirrors
that reflect your image.

08:08.780 --> 08:10.450
Meet people.

08:10.450 --> 08:12.190
Make friends.

08:12.190 --> 08:14.090
So that you can
know more about yourself.

08:15.690 --> 08:17.090
Gramps...

08:18.790 --> 08:21.200
W-W-What are you doing?

08:21.200 --> 08:23.560
I was just checking your temperature.

08:23.560 --> 08:24.830
I-I'm all right.

08:24.830 --> 08:26.600
Nothing's wrong with me.

08:26.600 --> 08:28.270
You were mumbling in your sleep.

08:28.270 --> 08:29.670
Who's Gramps?

08:29.670 --> 08:32.040
Gramps is Gramps.

08:32.040 --> 08:34.880
The man who raised me.

08:34.880 --> 08:36.140
Strange.

08:36.140 --> 08:40.110
A third class citizen in contact
with the first generation.

08:40.110 --> 08:42.820
Duero... was it?

08:42.820 --> 08:44.320
It's your turn now.

08:44.320 --> 08:45.650
I'd like you to come with me.

08:48.620 --> 08:50.660
The crystalline response is down 45%!

08:50.660 --> 08:52.360
The temperature's gone up 3 degrees!

08:52.360 --> 08:53.730
What happened?

08:53.730 --> 08:55.700
I don't know where
to start with this thing!

08:55.700 --> 08:57.030
Well, you know...

08:57.630 --> 08:58.670
And you?

08:58.670 --> 08:59.800
Hmm...

08:59.800 --> 09:02.140
What's with that "hmm..."?

09:02.140 --> 09:02.840
See?

09:02.840 --> 09:04.930
- Ill... Ill...
- Ill?

09:11.010 --> 09:12.910
She has a persisting light fever.

09:12.910 --> 09:14.350
Can you look at her?

09:14.350 --> 09:15.550
That's strange.

09:15.550 --> 09:19.720
I heard that women's medical
technology was advanced.

09:19.720 --> 09:21.620
Nothing less from an elite.

09:21.620 --> 09:24.760
You look for information even
during normal conversation.

09:24.760 --> 09:25.790
All right.

09:25.790 --> 09:29.660
Approximately 90% of this ship
cannot be controlled right now.

09:29.660 --> 09:32.400
That includes the medical systems.

09:32.400 --> 09:33.390
How's that?

09:34.900 --> 09:36.130
I'll look at the patient.

09:36.800 --> 09:37.770
Huh?

09:37.770 --> 09:39.010
What's wrong?

09:39.010 --> 09:40.740
I only see markers.

09:40.740 --> 09:42.840
Looks like something happened.

09:42.840 --> 09:43.880
No reason to stay.

09:43.880 --> 09:45.180
Let's get out of here.

09:45.180 --> 09:45.670
Roger!

09:52.190 --> 09:54.720
A nebula is now visible
ahead of the ship.

09:54.720 --> 09:56.420
We can't regain control!

09:56.420 --> 09:57.090
I swear.

09:57.090 --> 09:58.850
One thing after another!

09:59.360 --> 10:00.430
This is Meia.

10:00.430 --> 10:01.900
We're unable to launch the Dreads.

10:01.900 --> 10:03.100
We can't get them.

10:03.100 --> 10:05.500
We've been trapped
inside the elevator!

10:05.500 --> 10:06.660
Someone, help!

10:09.800 --> 10:11.640
We're going to plow in there?

10:11.640 --> 10:13.740
Idiot! Stop it!

10:13.740 --> 10:16.180
Stop!

10:22.650 --> 10:24.990
Engineering, I have a patient here.

10:24.990 --> 10:26.990
Make power to sick bay a priority.

10:26.990 --> 10:29.090
Who's saying that without
thinking about us?

10:29.090 --> 10:32.160
If we could read men's language,
we'd do it right now!

10:32.160 --> 10:33.560
I can read it.

10:35.600 --> 10:36.530
All right.

10:39.570 --> 10:40.840
Ow...

10:40.840 --> 10:42.770
At least put up a shield, dammit!

10:47.340 --> 10:48.340
A man?

10:48.340 --> 10:50.330
Oh, over here, over here!

10:51.710 --> 10:53.710
I want to know
the status of the Paksis,

10:53.710 --> 10:56.520
but I can't figure out this data!

10:56.520 --> 10:58.020
Hi-type #6.

10:58.020 --> 10:58.990
Why this?

10:58.990 --> 11:01.020
I don't know exactly why,

11:01.020 --> 11:04.190
but this thing and
Paksis' wavelengths are linked.

11:04.190 --> 11:07.460
That's why I thought
it would be a sensor, but...

11:07.460 --> 11:08.450
I see.

11:09.560 --> 11:10.900
How is it?

11:10.900 --> 11:13.970
Impurities are spreading
within the main engine room.

11:13.970 --> 11:17.170
It looks like a reaction
to the sudden changes.

11:17.170 --> 11:23.310
Originally, this system used
the energy from the crystal growth,

11:23.310 --> 11:25.750
but I've never seen
this reaction before.

11:25.750 --> 11:28.350
Could it be a result of the merger?

11:28.350 --> 11:29.420
Probably...

11:29.420 --> 11:31.150
Can you do something?

11:31.150 --> 11:33.890
I'm sorry, but I'm not an engineer.

11:33.890 --> 11:35.260
What are you saying?

11:35.260 --> 11:37.120
Everything that moves is alive!

11:37.120 --> 11:38.490
That's what I think.

11:38.490 --> 11:40.830
And it's a doctor's job
to fix all living things!

11:40.830 --> 11:41.820
Am I wrong?

11:42.830 --> 11:44.700
You say interesting things.

11:50.910 --> 11:53.770
All ship activity has ceased.

11:53.770 --> 11:55.610
Great, we finally stop,

11:55.610 --> 11:57.340
and it turns out to be a place like this?

11:58.810 --> 12:00.820
- Captain!
- Hmmm?

12:00.820 --> 12:03.080
A part of the ship has
started to transform again!

12:07.960 --> 12:10.690
The values for the ship
have started to shift.

12:10.690 --> 12:11.730
Here, too.

12:11.730 --> 12:13.790
What's happening?

12:13.790 --> 12:15.700
Pyoro!

12:15.700 --> 12:16.660
Ah...

12:16.660 --> 12:18.700
This brings me back to life!

12:18.700 --> 12:20.130
What is this thing?

12:20.130 --> 12:23.040
It might have something to do
with the nebula's composition.

12:23.040 --> 12:24.370
That's it!

12:24.370 --> 12:28.780
It's getting rid of the built-up
impurities and neutralizing it!

12:28.780 --> 12:30.080
Interesting.

12:30.080 --> 12:31.770
It really is behaving
like a living being.

12:42.120 --> 12:44.230
Captain, I have a suggestion.

12:44.230 --> 12:45.560
What is it?

12:45.560 --> 12:47.090
Upon checking the ship,

12:47.090 --> 12:50.430
it has been determined that
the male Vanguard can take off.

12:50.430 --> 12:51.700
So?

12:51.700 --> 12:56.840
I was thinking of using him
to search for Dita and Gascogne.

12:56.840 --> 12:58.510
Fine, go ahead.

12:58.510 --> 12:59.210
I will.

12:59.210 --> 13:02.000
By the way, what were you doing there?

13:03.710 --> 13:05.980
My duty is to support you, Captain.

13:05.980 --> 13:06.470
Out.

13:07.820 --> 13:09.370
It's no good!

13:10.120 --> 13:14.260
I can't believe I screwed up like this.

13:14.260 --> 13:15.120
Hold on.

13:15.120 --> 13:16.190
I'll get the Dread's tools.

13:16.190 --> 13:18.160
There's no need for that.

13:18.160 --> 13:19.460
Have you forgotten?

13:19.460 --> 13:20.930
This is work.

13:20.930 --> 13:22.660
Take the data and go back.

13:22.660 --> 13:24.800
But I can't leave you here, Ms. Gasco!

13:24.800 --> 13:26.830
Who said you were
leaving me to rot?

13:26.830 --> 13:28.570
This isn't some third-rate drama.

13:28.570 --> 13:30.500
I'm telling you
to get some help for us.

13:31.840 --> 13:33.210
Understood...

13:33.210 --> 13:35.200
I'll be back soon, so wait for me!

13:42.380 --> 13:43.540
They sure are pesky.

13:50.290 --> 13:51.560
Hot...

13:51.560 --> 13:53.690
My, what an outfit.

13:53.690 --> 13:56.000
What? Is it my turn now?

13:56.000 --> 13:57.500
On the contrary...

13:57.500 --> 13:59.400
I came here to ask a favor.

13:59.400 --> 14:00.230
A favor?

14:00.840 --> 14:02.340
I'll be honest.

14:02.340 --> 14:04.810
We left two of our crew behind.

14:04.810 --> 14:06.000
I'd like your help.

14:07.240 --> 14:11.010
What reason do
I have to help you guys?

14:11.010 --> 14:14.180
This isn't the time to
be talking about men or women.

14:14.180 --> 14:15.520
You saw it, right?

14:15.520 --> 14:17.250
That unknown enemy.

14:17.250 --> 14:21.120
I thought that since you defeated
them so easily the last time...

14:22.720 --> 14:25.090
The strong help the weak.

14:25.090 --> 14:28.530
I heard that was
common sense in a man's world.

14:28.530 --> 14:29.230
I see.

14:29.230 --> 14:30.460
All right!

14:30.460 --> 14:33.200
I showed you a side of me
that I didn't want to show.

14:33.200 --> 14:34.840
But this is the last time!

14:34.840 --> 14:37.400
I won't fall for your threats anymore!

14:37.400 --> 14:38.940
A threat?

14:38.940 --> 14:40.600
I never thought of it that way.

14:41.310 --> 14:43.680
No, the intake outtake ratio is off!

14:43.680 --> 14:45.750
It's because there
aren't enough link routes.

14:45.750 --> 14:47.920
But we can't put any
more burden on them!

14:47.920 --> 14:49.120
Don't give up.

14:49.120 --> 14:50.140
There must be a way!

14:52.050 --> 14:53.290
Detours!

14:53.290 --> 14:56.090
You end congestion
by opening a different path.

14:56.090 --> 14:58.490
A bypass? That's it!

14:58.490 --> 15:01.100
You'd make a great engineer!

15:01.100 --> 15:02.700
We're gonna get busy!

15:02.700 --> 15:04.030
Everyone, listen up!

15:08.270 --> 15:10.640
Proximity alert.

15:10.640 --> 15:12.270
What now?

15:12.270 --> 15:15.810
A body of ice the size
of an asteroid is approaching!

15:15.810 --> 15:16.580
You hear that?

15:16.580 --> 15:17.410
Do something!

15:18.680 --> 15:19.450
Stay away!

15:19.450 --> 15:20.850
Do something!

15:25.290 --> 15:26.010
No!

15:31.730 --> 15:33.390
What are they?

15:33.390 --> 15:35.730
They can regenerate
in these conditions?

15:39.370 --> 15:41.160
So I'm one of their ingredients?

15:45.340 --> 15:48.270
I hate annoying aliens!

15:50.080 --> 15:51.440
From the front, too?

16:00.520 --> 16:01.420
Damn it!

16:01.420 --> 16:04.260
Is this how you thank someone
who came to pick you up?

16:04.260 --> 16:05.160
Mr. Alien!

16:07.160 --> 16:08.160
She's...

16:08.160 --> 16:10.230
You came to save me!

16:10.230 --> 16:12.530
You really are a good alien!

16:12.530 --> 16:14.400
N-No, I'm not!

16:17.170 --> 16:17.940
Wow!

16:17.940 --> 16:20.070
What is this? Amazing!

16:20.070 --> 16:21.100
Hey, don't move!

16:22.110 --> 16:27.050
I really believed that you'd
come rescue me, Mr. Alien!

16:28.250 --> 16:30.150
I didn't come to rescue you.

16:30.150 --> 16:31.450
I was just looking for you.

16:32.650 --> 16:33.640
Thank you.

16:37.190 --> 16:39.230
You work rather well...

16:39.230 --> 16:41.220
I'd love to ask you to join us.

16:44.600 --> 16:46.260
So it's finally my turn?

16:55.480 --> 16:57.410
Putting it off till the last minute.

16:57.410 --> 16:59.980
What a great screenplay.

16:59.980 --> 17:03.050
We've somehow secured
up to Bypass #36.

17:03.050 --> 17:04.490
And you?

17:04.490 --> 17:06.280
I can't get anymore here.

17:07.150 --> 17:08.620
This will have to do.

17:08.620 --> 17:09.560
Impossible!

17:09.560 --> 17:12.290
If we don't do this right,
we'll lose even more balance!

17:13.160 --> 17:15.990
At times like these,
do you know what doctors do?

17:17.970 --> 17:20.570
We believe in the patients.

17:20.570 --> 17:21.900
Yeah...

17:21.900 --> 17:23.670
The ice mass is getting closer.

17:23.670 --> 17:25.210
The Paksis isn't responding!

17:25.210 --> 17:26.870
We're out of control!

17:30.440 --> 17:32.110
Distance is 12,000!

17:37.890 --> 17:39.510
We've regained control!

17:41.260 --> 17:43.360
Beep.

17:43.360 --> 17:44.880
I'm back now!

17:46.160 --> 17:47.330
We did it! We did it!

17:47.330 --> 17:48.450
We did it!

17:52.570 --> 17:54.300
Turn 30 degrees to the right!

17:54.300 --> 17:55.830
It's too late already!

18:01.980 --> 18:04.140
So I'm finally dead...

18:04.140 --> 18:05.670
...or not?

18:10.180 --> 18:13.350
Hmph, him again.

18:13.350 --> 18:16.160
- I'm so tired all of a sudden...
- See?

18:16.160 --> 18:17.690
See? Isn't this amazing?

18:17.690 --> 18:19.990
I get it, so get me off this thing!

18:27.230 --> 18:29.540
Upon conferring with the captain,

18:29.540 --> 18:33.610
we decided to inform the
entire crew about our situation.

18:33.610 --> 18:36.740
Upon analyzing the data
we got from the enemy debris,

18:36.740 --> 18:39.550
we found out a part
of the enemy structure.

18:39.550 --> 18:41.780
We would like you to look at this.

18:41.780 --> 18:43.450
This is the enemy's home planet.

18:43.450 --> 18:45.290
We don't know the location,

18:45.290 --> 18:47.650
but they seem to have
a lot of military power.

18:47.650 --> 18:49.490
- Strange planet!
- Sure is.

18:49.490 --> 18:52.690
We have entered the territory
of this unknown enemy,

18:52.690 --> 18:54.850
and are being attacked as invaders.

18:55.860 --> 18:58.700
During our journey back to Mejale space,

18:58.700 --> 19:02.340
we expect more battles with
the enemy for this same reason.

19:02.340 --> 19:04.270
Their objective, as we've found out,

19:04.270 --> 19:06.870
is to execute an operation

19:06.870 --> 19:11.180
which calls for the
razing of Mejale and Tarak.

19:11.180 --> 19:14.550
In other words,
the enemy is for some reason

19:14.550 --> 19:17.850
planning the destruction
of our home planet.

19:17.850 --> 19:19.590
We are pirates.

19:19.590 --> 19:22.020
We have no duty to Mejale or Tarak,

19:22.020 --> 19:25.430
however, it's not beneficial
to have someone we don't know

19:25.430 --> 19:27.630
destroy all of our great "customers."

19:27.630 --> 19:30.830
Therefore, I plan to return
home before the enemy arrives

19:30.830 --> 19:33.070
and inform them of this crisis.

19:33.070 --> 19:35.470
For this to happen,
we need to incorporate

19:35.470 --> 19:38.110
our captive men into the crew as well.

19:38.110 --> 19:39.640
What?

19:39.640 --> 19:41.480
So you finally understand.

19:41.480 --> 19:44.040
This ship and that large robot...

19:44.040 --> 19:46.280
There are many things
we don't understand.

19:46.280 --> 19:51.120
But we have to figure them
out one by one during our journey.

19:51.120 --> 19:53.850
I look forward to the
cooperation of the entire crew.

19:53.850 --> 19:54.820
That is all.

19:58.930 --> 20:00.390
I'm sorry.

20:00.390 --> 20:01.790
I'll go back to my station now.

20:02.600 --> 20:04.360
Do you know what caused your fever?

20:04.360 --> 20:06.670
W-Well, um...

20:06.670 --> 20:10.100
There is a parasitic organism
feeding on my patient's body.

20:10.100 --> 20:11.270
What?

20:11.270 --> 20:13.640
It's not that!

20:13.640 --> 20:14.710
I'm...

20:14.710 --> 20:17.640
...going to be having a baby.

20:17.640 --> 20:18.810
What?

20:18.810 --> 20:21.320
Ezra, when did you become a ferma?

20:21.320 --> 20:23.150
And who's the horma!

20:23.150 --> 20:26.620
I thought kids were made in factories?

20:26.620 --> 20:30.560
I did hear that women replicated
inside their bodies...

20:30.560 --> 20:33.090
I-I'm sorry, Captain.

20:33.090 --> 20:37.530
I was going to tell you after
that recent raid was done.

20:37.530 --> 20:40.900
There's nothing to apologize for, Ezra.

20:40.900 --> 20:43.200
I hope you have a healthy baby.

20:43.200 --> 20:44.540
Geez, Ezra.

20:44.540 --> 20:46.310
You didn't tell us anything.

20:46.310 --> 20:48.840
Hey, tell us. Who's the ohma?

20:48.840 --> 20:49.940
What is that?

20:49.940 --> 20:52.010
The ohma donates an egg

20:52.010 --> 20:54.580
and the ferma nurtures
it in her abdomen.

20:54.580 --> 20:56.380
You don't know anything, do you?

20:56.380 --> 20:57.620
This is the first I've heard...

20:57.620 --> 21:00.850
We really do have
a lot to be surprised about.

21:00.850 --> 21:02.860
Right, BC?

21:02.860 --> 21:04.590
Y-Yes, Captain.

21:04.590 --> 21:07.030
We have to do our share as well.

21:07.030 --> 21:10.600
Especially for the
new life that will be born.

21:10.600 --> 21:11.290
Yes.

21:12.930 --> 21:16.140
It looks like this
will be a long trip.

21:16.140 --> 21:17.800
Hey, Jura!

21:18.770 --> 21:21.380
When are we going
to get out of here?

21:21.380 --> 21:24.040
Someone, help us!

21:32.150 --> 21:37.760
Hey, you realized what the words,

21:37.760 --> 21:43.260
I really wanted to hear are, right?

21:43.260 --> 21:49.500
I was looking at your profile as
you talked about the distant future.

21:49.500 --> 21:59.810
Take me with you to the depths of dreams.

21:59.810 --> 22:02.350
Hey, with all of my body.

22:02.350 --> 22:14.130
A pistol named love shoots
through the center of my chest.

22:14.130 --> 22:25.740
Negotiations and common
sense hold no meaning at all.

22:25.740 --> 22:37.550
Pull the trigger named love and
shoot through my frozen heart.

22:37.550 --> 22:51.420
Pour in your love
to the tips of my fingers.
